 "method": "Same schedule as v40 with player 40 as the vacant slot (v40 is lane-exact for all 40, so the 39 real bowlers stay exact; that group plays three-handed). Lines of PG(3,3) (the 2-(40,4,1) design; points = GF(81)*/GF(3)* = Z_40 via x^4+x+2) resolved into 13 spreads by a parallelism invariant under the order-5 Singer subgroup n -> n+8: 3 fixed spreads (two line orbits each) + 2 spread orbits of length 5 (ext40/fable40/pg33.py enumerates all 176). Players = Z_5 x 8 classes, lane pairs = 2 tracks of 5, Z_5 rotates each track and the weeks together, so lane balance reduces to 8 classes x 10 lane pairs. Exact search (lz5b.c): choose the track of each base block (every class 5..8 visits per track), then the two tracks are independent small DFSs. 48 of the 176 parallelisms have an exact assignment (1-3 s each, exhaustive); this is parallelism #24. Lanes exact: every bowler on every lane pair 1 or 2 times. Week order: lambda=1, any order has prefix spread 1; positions by positions.assign.",
